 A QUIC proxy with pre-shared-key authentication. The server listens on a
 single UDP port, authenticates clients with a shared PSK over TLS 1.3, and
 dials the targets those clients ask for.
 .
 This package installs both ends:
 .
  * psk-server -- listens on UDP and connects to the requested targets;
  * psk-client -- opens a local SOCKS5 entry and forwards it over QUIC.
 .
 A systemd unit for the server is included. Startup arguments live in
 /etc/psk-quic-proxy/server.env (a dpkg conffile, so upgrades keep your edits).
 The service is not started on install: you must supply a PSK first.
